{
  "about": "Habit streak and month-grid vectors (OpenSpec change habits, design D3). Each case is a series with a rule and current due date, its occurrence records by date (done or skipped) and the device's today. stats is the expected habitStats (overdue: the current occurrence is before today; kept of keptOf, strength 0-100, atRisk and backOnTrack: habits-home D4) (null when the task cannot be measured); grids give the expected monthGrid states, one character per day of the month: '.' blank, D done, T tiny (habits-home: logged as the tiny version, counted as done), S skipped, M missed, P pending, U upcoming. A record written done>YYYY-MM-DD was moved to that day (the date it stands for stays its key); open is an open record (series-exceptions). split: the series is a piece of a split lineage (series-split D5) continuing the root described there (its rule, due, whether it reached its end and its records) from the date `from`.",
